  "summary": "The spoken homily and its source note pass. In Mark 13:33\u201337 and 14:29\u201340, Peter hears the command to watch, falls asleep and is still invited to pray. That sequence earns the invitation to keep a promised visit. I checked it against the study, the appointed Isaiah and Psalm, Jerome on Isaiah XVII, pp. 158\u2013159, Augustine on Psalm 79 \u00a7\u00a73 and 11, and the U.S. Collect and its commentary. The 1,104 words give an estimated 10 minutes 31 seconds at 105 words per minute. This was a silent reading."
